export anchor PixelCRTGameStyle:
    number: 292
    screen: CodeRepository
    name: Pixel CRT game
    idea: The pull request is laid out like an 8-bit adventure screen, with a coin-counter HUD, a menu cursor on the tabs, notched pixel-bordered dialog boxes, a checks health bar of twelve blocks, a reviewer party with pixel portraits and the changed files as inventory slots.
    base: dark
    palette:
        night: #100c24, the page and the style sheet background
        panel: #1e1840, dialog boxes and the style sheet cards
        slot: #2c2560, inventory slots, the hunk header, chips and the disabled merge button
        frame: #f2f0ff, pixel borders, main text and focus
        muted: #b9b2e6, secondary text and line numbers
        gold: #ffd23f, counters, the menu cursor, the primary button and requested changes
        hp: #4fe07a, health blocks, passed, approved, Open and added lines
        hurt: #ff6464, the broken health block, failing and removed lines
        sky: #6cb8ff, links and the linked issue
        pink: #ff8ad8, box titles
        ink: #100c24, text on gold, green and sky fills
    type:
        One monospace stack with a pixel font first, Press Start 2P, Lucida Console,
        DejaVu Sans Mono, ui-monospace. Dialog text 15px on 1.6 in normal case so it
        stays readable. The title 24px at 700. Box titles 16px caps tracked 0.1em in
        pink. HUD counters 14px at 700 caps. No smoothing tricks, only crisp shapes.
    layout:
        A 1160px game screen on a night background. A HUD bar runs across the top
        with a pixel B emblem, the owner and repository, a Private lock tag and
        three coin style counters for Watch 12, Star 48 and Fork 3. Under it the six
        tabs sit in a menu box with a gold arrow cursor beside Pull requests. The
        main area is a two column grid of notched pixel boxes. The wide Quest box
        holds the number 214, the title, the Open tag and the merge sentence spoken
        by a pixel portrait of Sam Ortiz. The narrow Party box lists Jonas Weber and
        Tomás Ruiz with pixel portraits and their verdicts. A full width HP box
        shows the twelve checks as health blocks, the failing block cracked with an
        x, and names e2e-android. The Inventory box shows the three files as square
        slots with counts, the Scroll box holds the diff with the comment as a
        speech bubble, and a Stats box lists assignees, labels, milestone and linked
        issue above a locked Merge button. Below 900px every box takes the full
        width.
    spacing: A 4px pixel unit. 20px box padding, 16px between boxes, 8px inside slots.
    density: Medium. Chunky boxes with a few items each.
    corners: Notched pixel corners made by stepping the border, never rounded.
    borders:
        4px frame borders drawn as stepped box shadows so the corners are notched,
        with a 4px dark inner line. Slots have 4px slot borders.
    shadows: A hard 4px drop step in black under boxes and buttons, no blur.
    icons:
        Pixel icons drawn on an 8 by 8 grid with crisp edges at 16px, always with a
        word. A pixel check for passed and approved, a pixel x for failing, a pixel
        triangle with a bang for requested changes, a pixel padlock for the blocked
        merge, a pixel eye, star and fork for the counters.
    focus: A 4px gold outline offset 4px with stepped corners.
    tone:
        Playful game labels for boxes, such as Quest, Party, HP and Inventory, with
        plain words for the content.
